# Glossary of Terms

## AI Participation
The ability for AI systems to consume, interpret, reason about, and operate on enterprise semantics and relationships.

## Attribute
A property or characteristic of an entity.

## Canonical
The authoritative or officially preferred definition or representation.

## Cardinality
Rules defining how many relationships may exist between entities.

## Classification
Grouping concepts into categories or hierarchies.

## Conceptual Ontology
A formal representation of conceptual meaning independent of implementation technology.

## Constraint
A rule limiting or governing valid semantics or behavior.

## Controlled Vocabulary
A governed set of approved terms and naming rules.

## Data Model
A structured representation of entities, attributes, and data structures.

## Dependency
A relationship where one entity relies on or affects another.

## Digital Thread
A connected network of lifecycle relationships linking engineering, manufacturing, verification, and operational information.

## Entity
A distinct conceptual or operational object represented in the model.

## Governance
The processes and rules used to maintain semantic consistency and authority.

## Inference
The ability to derive new conclusions from existing semantic relationships and rules.

## Logical Ontology
An ontology containing formal rules, constraints, and reasoning logic.

## MBSE
Model-Based Systems Engineering.

## Ontology
A formal representation of concepts, meaning, relationships, constraints, and semantics within a domain.

## Operational Ontology
An ontology actively integrated into enterprise systems, workflows, automation, and AI operations.

## Relationship Model
A model defining semantic relationships between entities.

## Semantic
Relating to meaning rather than merely structure or syntax.

## Semantic Graph
A network of interconnected entities and semantic relationships.

## Semantic Maturity
The degree to which enterprise meaning has been formalized, connected, governed, and operationalized.

## Structured Data
Information organized according to defined schemas and data structures.

## Systems Reasoning
Reasoning about dependencies, relationships, and behavior across interconnected systems.

## Taxonomy
A hierarchical classification system organizing concepts into categories.

## Traceability
The ability to follow relationships and dependencies across lifecycle artifacts.
